{"content_key": "apphy1-frq-039", "content_item_id": "68132f28-e9ca-44ef-ad80-1bc233070c7e", "content_item_version_id": "bf116285-ed24-4204-abb5-0991b3584a22", "version_num": 2, "full_text": "Response:\n(a) From 20.0=(1/2)(9.80)t², t=sqrt(40.0/9.80)=2.02 s. The impact speed is v=gt=(9.80)(2.02)=19.8 m/s downward. (b) With air resistance neglected, gravity is the only force, so Newton's second law gives the constant downward acceleration g throughout the fall.", "spans": [{"text": "Response:\n", "criterion_keys": [], "provenance": "authored_format", "source_field": null, "source_offset": null}, {"text": "(a) From 20.0=(1/2)(9.80)t², t=sqrt(40.0/9.80)=2.02 s. The impact speed is v=gt=(9.80)(2.02)=19.8 m/s downward. (b) With air resistance neglected, gravity is the only force, so Newton's second law gives the constant downward acceleration g throughout the fall.", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-speed", "part-a-time", "part-b"], "provenance": "authored", "source_field": "stem+stimulus+rubric+approved_fact_pack", "source_offset": null}], "coverage": {"criteria_total": 3, "criteria_covered": ["part-a-speed", "part-a-time", "part-b"], "criteria_uncovered": []}, "derivations": [{"value": "20.0", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-speed", "part-a-time", "part-b"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) From 20.0=(1/2)(9.80)t², t=sqrt(40.0/9.80)=2.02 s. The impact speed is v=gt=(9.80)(2.02)=19.8 m/s downward. (b) With air resistance neglected, gravity is the only force, so Newton's second law gives the constant downward acceleration g throughout the fall.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the time for the ball to reach the ground and its speed just before impact.\n\n(b) Explain why the ball's acceleration remains constant throughout the fall. A ball is dropped from rest from a height of 20.0 m above the ground (g = 9.80 m/s^2, ignore air resistance)."}