inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Determine the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, v0x and v0y. Before substituting any numbers, combine R = v0x t and t = 2v0y/g (with v0x = v0 cosθ, v0y = v0 sinθ) to derive the range symbolically as R = v0² sin(2θ)/g. Then use this relationship, together with H = v0y²/(2g), to calculate the maximum height, the total time of flight, and the horizontal range.\n\n(b) A second projectile is launched from the same location at the same initial speed, 25.0 m/s, but at 50.0° above the horizontal instead of 40.0°. Determine the range of this second launch and compare it to the range found in part (a). Then explain, in terms of the dependence of R on sin(2θ), why launching at 40° and at 50° (at the same speed) produces the same range. A projectile is launched from level ground at 25.0 m/s at an angle of 40.0° above the horizontal (g = 9.80 m/s^2, ignore air resistance)."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "180°", "criterion_keys": ["a-height", "a-range", "a-symbolic-range", "a-time", "b-50deg-range", "b-symmetry-explanation"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "computed", "expression": "(a) v0x=25.0 cos40.0° and v0y=25.0 sin40.0°. The maximum height is h=v0y²/(2g)=13.2 m, and flight time is t=2v0y/g=3.28 s. Combining R=v0x t with t=2v0y/g gives R=2v0xv0y/g=v0²sin(2θ)/g; thus R=(25.0²)sin80.0°/9.80=62.8 m. (b) At 50.0°, R=(25.0²)sin100°/9.80=62.8 m, exactly equal to the 40.0° range because 40° and 50° are complementary, their doubled angles are supplementary, and sin(180°-x)=sin x.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Determine the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, v0x and v0y. Before substituting any numbers, combine R = v0x t and t = 2v0y/g (with v0x = v0 cosθ, v0y = v0 sinθ) to derive the range symbolically as R = v0² sin(2θ)/g. Then use this relationship, together with H = v0y²/(2g), to calculate the maximum height, the total time of flight, and the horizontal range.\n\n(b) A second projectile is launched from the same location at the same initial speed, 25.0 m/s, but at 50.0° above the horizontal instead of 40.0°. Determine the range of this second launch and compare it to the range found in part (a). Then explain, in terms of the dependence of R on sin(2θ), why launching at 40° and at 50° (at the same speed) produces the same range. A projectile is launched from level ground at 25.0 m/s at an angle of 40.0° above the horizontal (g = 9.80 m/s^2, ignore air resistance)."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}], "confidence": "high", "flags": ["cross_criterion_entanglement"]}
{"content_key": "apphy1-frq-055", "content_item_id": "6e5b7671-b5b0-4e4f-a221-d771e3be97b6", "content_item_version_id": "c565c13b-b3b4-41f0-ab4c-206673372e1b", "version_num": 1, "full_text": "Response:\n(a) The radius is r=L sinθ=(1.20)sin25.0°=0.507 m. Vertical equilibrium gives T cosθ=mg, so T=(0.500)(9.80)/cos25.0°=5.41 N. (b) Horizontally, T sinθ=mv²/r, so v=sqrt(rg tanθ)=1.52 m/s. The period is T_p=2πr/v=2π(0.507)/1.52=2.09 s.", "spans": [{"text": "Response:\n", "criterion_keys": [], "provenance": "authored_format", "source_field": null, "source_offset": null}, {"text": "(a) The radius is r=L sinθ=(1.20)sin25.0°=0.507 m. Vertical equilibrium gives T cosθ=mg, so T=(0.500)(9.80)/cos25.0°=5.41 N. (b) Horizontally, T sinθ=mv²/r, so v=sqrt(rg tanθ)=1.52 m/s. The period is T_p=2πr/v=2π(0.507)/1.52=2.09 s.", "criterion_keys": ["a-radius", "a-tension", "b-period", "b-speed"], "provenance": "authored", "source_field": "stem+stimulus+rubric+approved_fact_pack", "source_offset": null}], "coverage": {"criteria_total": 4, "criteria_covered": ["a-radius", "a-tension", "b-period", "b-speed"], "criteria_uncovered": []}, "derivations": [{"value": "1.20", "criterion_keys": ["a-radius", "a-tension", "b-period", "b-speed"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) The radius is r=L sinθ=(1.20)sin25.0°=0.507 m. Vertical equilibrium gives T cosθ=mg, so T=(0.500)(9.80)/cos25.0°=5.41 N. (b) Horizontally, T sinθ=mv²/r, so v=sqrt(rg tanθ)=1.52 m/s. The period is T_p=2πr/v=2π(0.507)/1.52=2.09 s.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the tension in the string and the radius of the ball's circular path.\n\n(b) Calculate the ball's speed and the period of its circular motion. A 0.500 kg ball attached to a 1.20 m string moves in a horizontal circle as a conical pendulum, with the string making a 25.0° angle with the vertical (g = 9.80 m/s^2)."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "5.0°", "criterion_keys": ["a-radius", "a-tension", "b-period", "b-speed"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) The radius is r=L sinθ=(1.20)sin25.0°=0.507 m. Vertical equilibrium gives T cosθ=mg, so T=(0.500)(9.80)/cos25.0°=5.41 N. (b) Horizontally, T sinθ=mv²/r, so v=sqrt(rg tanθ)=1.52 m/s. The period is T_p=2πr/v=2π(0.507)/1.52=2.09 s.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the tension in the string and the radius of the ball's circular path.\n\n(b) Calculate the ball's speed and the period of its circular motion. A 0.500 kg ball attached to a 1.20 m string moves in a horizontal circle as a conical pendulum, with the string making a 25.0° angle with the vertical (g = 9.80 m/s^2)."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "0.507", "criterion_keys": ["a-radius", "a-tension", "b-period", "b-speed"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "computed", "expression": "(a) The radius is r=L sinθ=(1.20)sin25.0°=0.507 m. Vertical equilibrium gives T cosθ=mg, so T=(0.500)(9.80)/cos25.0°=5.41 N. (b) Horizontally, T sinθ=mv²/r, so v=sqrt(rg tanθ)=1.52 m/s. The period is T_p=2πr/v=2π(0.507)/1.52=2.09 s.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the tension in the string and the radius of the ball's circular path.\n\n(b) Calculate the ball's speed and the period of its circular motion. A 0.500 kg ball attached to a 1.20 m string moves in a horizontal circle as a conical pendulum, with the string making a 25.0° angle with the vertical (g = 9.80 m/s^2)."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pac