{"content_key": "apphy1-frq-np1-002", "content_item_id": "383ad75c-6ebb-4383-9a1e-6d8756f548ff", "content_item_version_id": "4c413573-a128-4274-a44c-2bacd6289897", "version_num": 2, "full_text": "Response:\n(a) The velocity-time slope is a=(0-4)/(4-0)=-1 m/s². (b) Displacement is the triangular area under the graph: (1/2)(4 s)(4 m/s)=8 m. (c) From 0 to 4 s, position rises but is concave down because its positive slope (velocity) decreases to zero. From 4 to 6 s the position graph is horizontal because velocity is zero. (d) From 4 to 6 s, a=0 because velocity is constant.", "spans": [{"text": "Response:\n", "criterion_keys": [], "provenance": "authored_format", "source_field": null, "source_offset": null}, {"text": "(a) The velocity-time slope is a=(0-4)/(4-0)=-1 m/s². (b) Displacement is the triangular area under the graph: (1/2)(4 s)(4 m/s)=8 m. (c) From 0 to 4 s, position rises but is concave down because its positive slope (velocity) decreases to zero. From 4 to 6 s the position graph is horizontal because velocity is zero. (d) From 4 to 6 s, a=0 because velocity is constant.", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "provenance": "authored", "source_field": "stem+stimulus+rubric+approved_fact_pack", "source_offset": null}], "coverage": {"criteria_total": 4, "criteria_covered": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "criteria_uncovered": []}, "derivations": [{"value": "0", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) The velocity-time slope is a=(0-4)/(4-0)=-1 m/s². (b) Displacement is the triangular area under the graph: (1/2)(4 s)(4 m/s)=8 m. (c) From 0 to 4 s, position rises but is concave down because its positive slope (velocity) decreases to zero. From 4 to 6 s the position graph is horizontal because velocity is zero. (d) From 4 to 6 s, a=0 because velocity is constant.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the object's acceleration during the interval 0 < t < 4 s.\n\n(b) Calculate the object's displacement during the interval 0 <= t <= 4 s.\n\n(c) Describe the shape of the object's position-time graph over the full 0 <= t <= 6 s interval, and explain your reasoning.\n\n(d) State the object's acceleration during the interval 4 s < t < 6 s. A velocity-time graph shows an object's velocity decreasing linearly from 4 m/s at t = 0 s to 0 m/s at t = 4 s. From t = 4 s to t = 6 s, the object's velocity remains constant at 0 m/s."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "4", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) The velocity-time slope is a=(0-4)/(4-0)=-1 m/s². (b) Displacement is the triangular area under the graph: (1/2)(4 s)(4 m/s)=8 m. (c) From 0 to 4 s, position rises but is concave down because its positive slope (velocity) decreases to zero. From 4 to 6 s the position graph is horizontal because velocity is zero. (d) From 4 to 6 s, a=0 because velocity is constant.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Answer all parts of the following question.\n\n(a) Calculate the object's acceleration during the interval 0 < t < 4 s.\n\n(b) Calculate the object's displacement during the interval 0 <= t <= 4 s.\n\n(c) Describe the shape of the object's position-time graph over the full 0 <= t <= 6 s interval, and explain your reasoning.\n\n(d) State the object's acceleration during the interval 4 s < t < 6 s. A velocity-time graph shows an object's velocity decreasing linearly from 4 m/s