{"content_key": "apphy1-frq-np1-004", "content_item_id": "58aac6ec-e5bd-4577-93ec-c9718bd8b4a8", "content_item_version_id": "91ea2d10-2353-4956-a83a-6f0be6d6f6fd", "version_num": 2, "full_text": "Response:\n(a) N=mg=(5)(10)=50 N. (b) Since the block is moving, f_k=μ_kN=(0.2)(50)=10 N opposite the motion. (c) F_net,x=20-10=10 N. (d) a=F_net/m=10/5=2 m/s² in the applied-force direction.", "spans": [{"text": "Response:\n", "criterion_keys": [], "provenance": "authored_format", "source_field": null, "source_offset": null}, {"text": "(a) N=mg=(5)(10)=50 N. (b) Since the block is moving, f_k=μ_kN=(0.2)(50)=10 N opposite the motion. (c) F_net,x=20-10=10 N. (d) a=F_net/m=10/5=2 m/s² in the applied-force direction.", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "provenance": "authored", "source_field": "stem+stimulus+rubric+approved_fact_pack", "source_offset": null}], "coverage": {"criteria_total": 4, "criteria_covered": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "criteria_uncovered": []}, "derivations": [{"value": "5", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) N=mg=(5)(10)=50 N. (b) Since the block is moving, f_k=μ_kN=(0.2)(50)=10 N opposite the motion. (c) F_net,x=20-10=10 N. (d) a=F_net/m=10/5=2 m/s² in the applied-force direction.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Assume the block is moving in the direction of the applied 20 N force throughout.\n\nAnswer all parts of the following question. Use g = 10 m/s^2.\n\n(a) Calculate the magnitude of the normal force exerted on the block by the surface.\n\n(b) Calculate the magnitude of the kinetic friction force acting on the block.\n\n(c) Calculate the net force acting on the block in the horizontal direction.\n\n(d) Calculate the magnitude of the block's acceleration. A 5 kg block on a horizontal surface is pulled by a horizontal applied force of 20 N. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the surface is 0.2, and the block is already moving."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "10", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "given", "expression": "(a) N=mg=(5)(10)=50 N. (b) Since the block is moving, f_k=μ_kN=(0.2)(50)=10 N opposite the motion. (c) F_net,x=20-10=10 N. (d) a=F_net/m=10/5=2 m/s² in the applied-force direction.", "inputs": [{"label": "stored stem and stimulus", "value": "see source_quote", "source_quote": "Assume the block is moving in the direction of the applied 20 N force throughout.\n\nAnswer all parts of the following question. Use g = 10 m/s^2.\n\n(a) Calculate the magnitude of the normal force exerted on the block by the surface.\n\n(b) Calculate the magnitude of the kinetic friction force acting on the block.\n\n(c) Calculate the net force acting on the block in the horizontal direction.\n\n(d) Calculate the magnitude of the block's acceleration. A 5 kg block on a horizontal surface is pulled by a horizontal applied force of 20 N. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the surface is 0.2, and the block is already moving."}, {"label": "governing relations", "value": "see approved fact pack", "source_quote": "docs/product/AP_PHYSICS_1_CED_FACT_PACK.md"}]}, {"value": "50", "criterion_keys": ["part-a-criterion-01", "part-b-criterion-01", "part-c-criterion-01", "part-d-criterion-01"], "span_index": 1, "kind": "computed", "expression": "(a) N=mg=(5)(10)=50 N. (b) Since the block is moving, f_k=μ_kN=(0.2)(50)=10 N opposite the motion. (c) F_net,x=20-10=10 N. (d) a=F_net/m=10/5=2 m/s² in the applied-force direction.", "inputs": [{"labe